# libmpg123 1.26.2 — our delta from pristine upstream.
#
# Upstream: https://www.mpg123.de/download/mpg123-1.26.2.tar.bz2
#           sha256 00f7bf7ea64fcec2c9d07751d6ad8849343ee09c282ea3b0d5dd486e886e2ff3
# Apply from the SPLIT tree (see below): a/<f> paths under sdk/lib/3rdparty/libmpg123/,
# a/include/<f> paths under sdk/include/reactos/libs/libmpg123/.
#
# THIS IS A MIXED-VINTAGE DROP, WHICH IS THE HEADLINE FINDING.
# Everything is 1.26.2 EXCEPT src/compat/compat.c, which is a verbatim OLDER UPSTREAM
# FILE. Measured against every release in range, normalized:
#       1.23.8 -> 469 lines    1.24.0 -> 0    1.25.10 -> 0    1.25.13 -> 0
#       1.26.0 -> 219          1.26.1 -> 219  1.26.2 -> 219
# Zero against the whole 1.24.0-1.25.13 span, and its banner reads "copyright 2007-2016"
# where 1.26.2 reads "2007-2020". So the 219-line compat.c hunk below is NOT a ReactOS
# edit — it is upstream's own 1.25->1.26 change, absent because the file was never
# refreshed. Do not "revert" it thinking you are removing a local patch.
#
# THE CONSEQUENCE IS A LATENT INCONSISTENCY, currently harmless:
# compat.h IS 1.26.2 vintage and declares `size_t unintr_fwrite(...)`, and intsym.h
# mangles it to INT123_unintr_fwrite — but the stale compat.c never defines it. Nothing
# in the tree calls it (grepped both halves), so it is a dead declaration rather than a
# link error today. Re-syncing compat.c to 1.26.2 would fix the skew and the declaration
# in one go; it also needs upstream's wpathconv.h, whose content our older compat.c
# carries INLINE rather than #included. Flagged, not done: this pass records state.
#
# EVERYTHING ELSE IS SMALL:
#   parse.c      6 lines, a pure __REACTOS__ guard that only moves `#include "getbits.h"`.
#   mpg123.h     16 lines: the expected @PACKAGE_VERSION@/@API_VERSION@ substitution from
#                mpg123.h.in (1.26.2 / 45), plus a __REACTOS__-guarded `typedef long
#                ssize_t` replacing the MSVC ptrdiff_t one.
#   compat.h     6 lines: the same ssize_t guard, plus two dead msdn.microsoft.com doc
#                URLs updated to learn.microsoft.com.
#   optimize.h   4 lines: __declspec(align) vs __attribute__((aligned)).
#
# NOT IN THIS PATCH (no upstream counterpart): precomp.h (our PCH) and config.h (ours;
# upstream generates it). config.h selects the generic-C OPT_I386 path with
# REAL_IS_FLOAT — no asm, no MMX/SSE/AltiVec — all three layers, ID3v2, ICY, gapless and
# the new Huffman tables, WANT_WIN32_UNICODE/SOCKETS on, USE_MODULES off. Usermode only:
# there is no DbgPrint/kernel shim here, unlike libsamplerate's config.h.
#
# 37 further files differ ONLY by trailing-whitespace stripping (24 in the library half,
# 13 in the include half) and are excluded, so pristine + this patch does NOT reproduce
# the tree byte-for-byte. Re-check with the normalized diff:
#   diff -a <(sed -e 's/\r$//' -e 's/[[:space:]]*$//' A) <(sed -e 's/\r$//' -e 's/[[:space:]]*$//' B)
#
# SECURITY: the decoder is untouched. layer1/2/3.c, id3.c, huffman.h, newhuffman.h,
# frame.c, format.c, readers.c and the body of parse.c are byte-identical or
# whitespace-only against pristine 1.26.2. No bounds check, allocation, buffer size or
# Huffman/ID3 logic differs. The only functional-content difference in the compiled set
# is compat.c's EINTR retry plumbing, which is I/O, not parsing.
#
